{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00368",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 3.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. It's my turn, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.6,
      "end_seconds": 7.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.58,
      "end_seconds": 18.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Mainly fever and chills. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.43,
      "end_seconds": 20.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.01,
      "end_seconds": 28.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "For two days, I'd say. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.48,
      "end_seconds": 43.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.58,
      "end_seconds": 59.41,
      "duration_seconds": 15.83,
      "text": "Well, it's mild, honestly. It's a few times a day. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. Well, I've had shortness of breath too, for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.97,
      "end_seconds": 74.5,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.07,
      "end_seconds": 78.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.6,
      "end_seconds": 82.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Have you had any vomiting, leg swelling or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.18,
      "end_seconds": 87.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting, leg swelling or palpitations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.6,
      "end_seconds": 96.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any coughing up blood or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.97,
      "end_seconds": 100.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, no coughing up blood or confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.11,
      "end_seconds": 103.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.82,
      "end_seconds": 107.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.3,
      "end_seconds": 109.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.83,
      "end_seconds": 112.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "I, I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.06,
      "end_seconds": 117.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.19,
      "end_seconds": 121.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.27,
      "end_seconds": 123.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.87,
      "end_seconds": 145.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.12,
      "end_seconds": 162.38,
      "duration_seconds": 15.26,
      "text": "So, I take Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I took the morning off to come in today. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.69,
      "end_seconds": 170.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "So, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.97,
      "end_seconds": 173.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Yes, codeine. I get vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.42,
      "end_seconds": 178.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.73,
      "end_seconds": 179.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.02,
      "end_seconds": 192.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.02,
      "end_seconds": 206.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.3,
      "end_seconds": 231.41,
      "duration_seconds": 10.11,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 94 percent on room air, respiratory rate 23, heart rate 95, pressure 129 over 90, temp 37.0 degrees. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.69,
      "end_seconds": 247.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.58,
      "text": "Not really, you know, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.41,
      "end_seconds": 251.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.93,
      "end_seconds": 253.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.89,
      "end_seconds": 257.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.11,
      "end_seconds": 268.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Breathing rate is a bit fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.29,
      "end_seconds": 275.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.88,
      "end_seconds": 288.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.95,
      "end_seconds": 312.77,
      "duration_seconds": 23.82,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with a possible pneumonia on the right side at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out a pulmonary embolism yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had fever and chills for two days, mild, and no leg swelling or coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.12,
      "end_seconds": 315.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.08,
      "end_seconds": 333.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.57,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for infection. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Let's get a chest X-ray, for suspected pneumonia. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.13,
      "end_seconds": 346.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.81,
      "text": "Let's use paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. You take it by mouth. That should help with fever and body aches. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.46,
      "end_seconds": 350.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.1,
      "end_seconds": 375.45,
      "duration_seconds": 23.35,
      "text": "Rest and fluids, and finish every dose of the antibiotic. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Please don't sit on it if the breathlessness worsens or you become drowsy. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.06,
      "end_seconds": 376.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.81,
      "end_seconds": 380.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the X-ray."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.68,
      "end_seconds": 385.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.46,
      "end_seconds": 391.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.25,
      "end_seconds": 400.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed and come back after the X-ray. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.21,
      "end_seconds": 403.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.51,
      "end_seconds": 406.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}